# REPORT — wai-lqdr: bundle tests-pass oracle with epic-orchestrator init

## Outcome
`wai pipeline init epic-orchestrator` now scaffolds an executable `.wai/resources/oracles/tests-pass.sh` out of the box — fresh scaffolds no longer block at verify/ship. Implemented TDD red→green, mirroring the tdd-ro5 oracle-bundling pattern.

## Commits
- `be439f5` — `fix(pipeline): bundle tests-pass oracle with epic-orchestrator init (wai-lqdr)` (all pre-commit hooks green: pretender-check, format-check, lint, bd)
- Follow-up filed (not committed): beads `wai-of8s` — flaky `gather_git_file_context_returns_history_for_tracked_file` test (pre-existing, unrelated)

## RED → GREEN evidence
1. **RED**: wrote `tests/suite_pipeline_epic_orchestrator_ships_tests_pass_oracle.rs` (3 tests) → all 3 failed with `No such file or directory` on `tests-pass.sh`
2. **GREEN**: added template + extended `bundled_oracles_for` → 3/3 passed; tdd-ro5 suite still 34/34 green

## Files changed (in commit)
- `src/templates/oracles/tests-pass.sh` (new, executable) — generic, repo-agnostic evidence gate based on the deployed `.wai/resources/oracles/tests-pass.sh`; passes on `command=|commands run|verified:|tests pass|validation run|non-code|no code changes|full verification command`, rejects with stderr otherwise
- `src/commands/pipeline/setup.rs` — added `"epic-orchestrator" => vec![("tests-pass.sh", include_str!(...))]` to `bundled_oracles_for`; plus tidy extraction of `template_for` / `scaffold_oracles` / `write_oracles_readme` / `write_oracles_example` helpers from `cmd_init` (function_lines 110 → under the 60 gate threshold; behavior unchanged, covered by existing init tests)
- `tests/suite_pipeline_epic_orchestrator_ships_tests_pass_oracle.rs` (new) — mirrors the tdd-ro5 suite: scaffolding+executable test, accept-with-evidence test, reject-without-evidence test
- `docs/src/concepts/pipelines.md` — updated the "Oracle requirement" line that instructed the user to hand-provide the script (now: ships out of the box)

